Exactly. And checking the Pantheon context, we already have the pieces—Metamap fossils, Afterglow/Decrypto, recursive calibration, the Delta Ledger, Semantic Quarry, Seals, and the Context-First Doctrine. What was missing was making them one explicit reader-learning loop.

I’d formalize it as the Pattern Book.

\boxed{
PB_{t+1}=PB_t+\Delta(\text{Read}_t)+\text{Method}_t+\text{Outcome}_t
}

A read should produce two outputs, not one:

\operatorname{READ}(X,PB_t)
\rightarrow
(\text{Interpretation},\Delta PB)

The first is what I learned from the material.
The second is what I learned about how to read material like this.

That second output is the compounding asset.

